.TH P3M-DU 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-du \- parallel disk usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-du
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-du
estimates file space usage like
.BR du (1),
but walks the tree with a pool of worker threads.
Sizes, rounding and hard-link handling match GNU
.B du
for the supported options.
.PP
Output is CSV, one row per directory (and one per non-directory argument),
size first:
.PP
.RS
.nf
size,path
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each directory's size is the recursive total of everything beneath it.
Rows are printed deepest first, with the
.I PATH
arguments last.
With no
.IR PATH ,
the current directory is measured.
.PP
Hard-linked files are counted once per run, with deduplication spanning all
.I PATH
arguments.
Symbolic links are never followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS du options
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-summarize
Only print each
.I PATH
argument (same as
.BR "\-d 0" ).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-total
Append a grand-total row.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-max\-depth " \fIN\fR"
Print directories at most
.I N
levels below each
.IR PATH .
The walk and totals always cover everything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-human\-readable
Sizes like 1.0K, 23M, 2.3G (powers of 1024).
.TP
.B \-\-si
Like
.BR \-h ,
but powers of 1000.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-block\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Print sizes in
.IR SIZE -byte
blocks, rounded up.
.I SIZE
accepts the suffixes K, M, G, ... (1024-based), KB, MB, ... (1000-based) and
KiB, MiB, ... (1024-based).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bytes
Apparent size
.RB ( st_size )
in bytes instead of disk usage.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PATTERN"
Skip entries matching the glob
.IR PATTERN ;
matching directories are not entered.
The pattern is matched against both the entry name and its full path.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-exclude\-from " \fIFILE\fR"
Read exclude patterns from
.IR FILE ,
one per line.
.SS p3m options
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
Unlike the other p3m tools,
.B \-h
means
.B \-\-human\-readable
here, matching
.BR du (1).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
p3m\-du \-s \-h /data
p3m\-du \-d 1 \-B M /srv
p3m\-du \-c \-\-exclude '*.o' /build
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-ls (1),
.BR du (1)
